WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.580
To manage this balance, the European
scientific community relies on

2
00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.080
the Aaliyah Code of Conduct.

3
00:00:05.679 --> 00:00:10.080
These four quadrants represent the foundational
standards for professional research integrity.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:15.259
They demand reliability in research
design, honesty in communicating results,

5
00:00:16.259 --> 00:00:20.199
respect for participants and ecosystems,
and accountability for the entire

6
00:00:20.199 --> 00:00:21.199
life cycle.

7
00:00:21.339 --> 00:00:25.320
When those virtues fail, researchers cross
into professional misconduct.

8
00:00:25.979 --> 00:00:30.800
This graphic outlines the FFP spectrum,
the absolute boundaries of

9
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:31.800
scientific integrity.

10
00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.399
The first violation is fabrication, the
total invention of data

11
00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:38.419
or results and reporting them as true.

12
00:00:38.419 --> 00:00:43.539
The second is falsification, the
manipulation of equipment or the

13
00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:46.619
unjustified alteration and suppression of
existing data.

14
00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:49.020
The third is plagiarism.

15
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:53.600
And alongside these core three, the
spectrum includes secondary breaches

16
00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.919
like exploitative authorship practices and
severe data mismanagement.

17
00:00:57.919 --> 00:01:00.000
Any FFP violation introduces false
variables into the shared evidence base,
